diff --git a/saas/README.md b/saas/README.md
index 28b0891..b227183 100644
--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -40,6 +40,32 @@ bin/dev # You need to start the dev server in the same terminal session
 
 This will ask for your 1password authorization to read and set the environment variables that Stripe needs.
 
+### How billing works
+
+Plans are defined in `app/models/plan.rb`:
+
+| Plan         | Price     | Cards     | Storage |
+|--------------|-----------|-----------|---------|
+| Free         | $0        | 1,000     | 1 GB    |
+| Unlimited    | $20/month | Unlimited | 5 GB    |
+| Unlimited+   | $25/month | Unlimited | 500 GB  |
+
+Stripe hosts checkout and the customer portal. Account admins upgrade from the account settings, which sends them to Stripe Checkout; subscribers manage payment details, switch plans, and cancel in the portal. Stripe reports subscription changes to `POST /stripe/webhooks`, and that's what moves an account between plans.
+
+Each environment needs:
+
+* `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`
+* `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, the signing secret of the webhook endpoint. Without it, every webhook is refused.
+* `STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID` and `STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID`, the Unlimited and Unlimited+ prices. A price whose lookup key is the plan key (`monthly_v1`, `monthly_extra_storage_v1`) is recognized too.
+
+In the Stripe dashboard, the webhook endpoint must send the `customer.subscription.created`, `.updated`, `.deleted`, `.paused`, and `.resumed` events, and the customer portal must allow switching between the two prices.
+
+A free account that runs out of cards can keep drafting, but can't publish or create cards through the API. Deleting an account cancels its subscription.
+
+### Support tools
+
+Staff can find accounts at `/admin/accounts`. An account's page can comp it (a free Unlimited plan) and override the card count and bytes used its limits are measured against.
+
 ### Stripe environments
 
 * [Development](https://dashboard.stripe.com/acct_1SdTFtRus34tgjsJ/test/dashboard)
